---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AdSlot from '../components/common/AdSlot.astro';

const privacySchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  'name': 'Privacy Policy - Text to Handwriting',
  'description': 'Read the Text to Handwriting Privacy Policy. Learn about our local browser-only data processing model, cookies, and analytics policies.'
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - Text to Handwriting"
  description="Read the Text to Handwriting privacy policy. Learn how all text-to-handwriting and signature generation is processed completely client-side in your browser."
  activeTab="privacy"
  schema={privacySchema}
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
    <AdSlot slotId="header-leaderboard" />

    <div class="border-b border-hairline pb-4 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-primary uppercase font-mono">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-mute font-mono mt-1">Effective Date: June 12, 2026. Your privacy is our priority.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-xs md:text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        At Text to Handwriting, we take your privacy seriously. This Privacy Policy explains our practices regarding the collection, use, disclosure, and protection of information when you use our online text-to-handwriting conversion tools, signature generators, and related services.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary font-mono uppercase tracking-tight">1. Client-Side Processing (Zero Uploads)</h2>
      <p>
        The core architecture of Text to Handwriting is designed to be <strong>entirely client-side</strong>. This means:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>No Text Uploads:</strong> Any paragraphs, letters, or assignments you type or paste into our editor are processed directly in your web browser. We never upload your text to external servers.</li>
        <li><strong>No Image Uploads:</strong> When you insert custom diagrams, drawings, or background paper images, the file reading and canvas composition happen locally using your browser's APIs (FileReader, HTML5 Canvas). No images are saved or transmitted to our servers.</li>
        <li><strong>No Signature Uploads:</strong> Handwritten signatures drawn on the canvas or typed signatures remain fully isolated within your browser's local sandbox memory.</li>
        <li><strong>Local PDF Compiler:</strong> Compiled PDFs and ZIP packages are generated locally using <code>pdf-lib</code> and <code>JSZip</code> directly inside your browser window.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary font-mono uppercase tracking-tight">2. Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        Although we do not upload or monitor your documents, we may collect minimal data to maintain page performance and support basic site operations:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Usage Statistics:</strong> We may use basic, privacy-friendly analytics to count page views and gather aggregate traffic details (such as browser type, operating system version, and general geography) to optimize site styling and loading speeds.</li>
        <li><strong>Local Storage:</strong> We may use your browser's local storage to save your editor configuration settings (such as default font size, margin width, line spacing, and pen color) for convenience when you return to the page.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary font-mono uppercase tracking-tight">3. Cookies and Advertising Technology</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small data files stored on your device when you visit websites. We use cookies, local storage, and related web technologies to optimize your experience:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Functional Local Storage:</strong> Remembers your editor configuration, selected handwriting font, page size, margin offsets, and pen color so you do not have to reconfigure them on every visit.</li>
        <li><strong>Third-Party Advertising Cookies:</strong> Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to our website or other websites on the Internet.</li>
        <li><strong>Performance Analytics:</strong> Aggregates anonymized performance metrics to ensure fast canvas compilation speeds across mobile and desktop devices.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary font-mono uppercase tracking-tight">4. Google AdSense & Third-Party Advertising Disclosures</h2>
      <p>
        We monetize our free educational tools using Google AdSense. In compliance with Google Publisher Policies, please note the following required disclosures:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>DART Cookie Usage:</strong> Google's use of advertising cookies (including the DoubleClick DART cookie) enables it and its partners to serve targeted advertisements to users based on their visits to Text to Handwriting and/or other websites on the Internet.</li>
        <li><strong>Opting Out of Personalized Ads:</strong> Users may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline font-semibold">Google Ads Settings</a>. Alternatively, you can opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline font-semibold">www.aboutads.info</a> or the <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline font-semibold">Network Advertising Initiative Consumer Opt-Out Page</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Third-Party Vendors:</strong> Third-party ad networks and ad servers may also set cookies to measure ad performance and personalize content. We have no direct control over cookies set by third-party advertisers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary font-mono uppercase tracking-tight">5. GDPR and International User Rights</h2>
      <p>
        For visitors located in the European Economic Area (EEA), United Kingdom, or Switzerland:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Right to Consent:</strong> You have the right to accept or decline non-essential advertising cookies via our interactive Cookie Preference banner.</li>
        <li><strong>Data Minimization:</strong> Because all document processing, font rendering, and PDF exports are processed locally in your browser sandbox, no personally identifiable document content is stored on our servers.</li>
        <li><strong>Data Access & Portability:</strong> Any content created on our site remains entirely on your local machine and can be exported or deleted at your discretion by clearing your browser cache.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary font-mono uppercase tracking-tight">6. CCPA / CPRA Compliance (California Residents)</h2>
      <p>
        Under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), California residents have specific rights regarding their personal data:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>No Sale of Personal Information:</strong> We do not sell, rent, or trade user document data, handwriting signatures, or personal content.</li>
        <li><strong>Opt-Out Rights:</strong> You can opt out of third-party interest-based advertising cookies using the opt-out links listed above in Section 4.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary font-mono uppercase tracking-tight">7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy periodically to align with evolving web standards and ad network requirements. Changes will be published directly on this page with a revised effective date.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-primary font-mono uppercase tracking-tight">8. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        For inquiries regarding our privacy standards, cookie consent architecture, or client-side processing, reach out through our <a href="/contact-us" class="text-link hover:underline font-semibold">Contact Us</a> page or email <code>privacy@texttohandwriting.me</code>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <AdSlot slotId="footer-leaderboard" />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
